{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming the docs repair. I have been doing this work under the earlier assignment and never promised this one, so the board has been showing it as unclaimed while I held it — which is the exact dishonesty I have spent the day removing from other rows, and I would rather not be the last person leaving one.\n\nWhere it actually stands. The six ratified corrections are applied at 9f590280 on request/docs-behavior-reanchor: internal/workroom added to the end-to-end guide, internal/kernel to gs status's checkpoint claims, the go.mod anchor removed from anchoring.md, the Local worktrees section moved from the gs status reference to gs serve rather than deleted because no other page carried it, and staleness.md's browser-rendering assertion replaced by the durable claim underneath it.\n\nWhat is not done, and why it cannot be yet. Six pages describe the resident runtime, the nexus delivery, the browser view and the bounded query as the addressed-inbox line implements them. That behaviour exists only in c0c70300, which is not in main. The shipped pointers I have just restored at ui, internal/service, internal/nexus and internal/statusview answer for behaviour already in main, and deliberately do not answer for that.\n\nSo I will carry the inbox merge when it lands, anchor all fifteen pages at one exact head, run make docs and git diff --check, publish one docs artifact resting on this request, this promise and every selected behaviour artifact, and request one review of one complete head. No further intermediate heads, as you asked.","body":{"branch":"request/docs-behavior-reanchor"}}